    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the full `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` field so it's `true` when more than 80 owners were already created for the same day, otherwise `false`.\n\nThe field is a creation-time snapshot (like the existing `namesakeCount`), so it's computed on create, stored, and returned unchanged on later reads. Changes:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 reused the already-computed `registeredOnDay` count (owners with the same registration/business day) and set `bulkSignupWarning = registeredOnDay > 80` on the owner before saving. This shares the exact accumulation path as the daily-registration-limit rule.\n- The MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps the field automatically by name (no explicit mapping needed).\n\nThe `>80` threshold sits below the existing hard daily limit of 100, so warnings surface for the 81\u201399 range. Tests: `AcceptanceTest` passes (`bulkSignupWarning` is `false` for a fresh create) and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
